licenses. We have attempted to list all of these third-party libraries and
their licenses below (the most up-to-date information can be found by
inspecting the metadata of each installed package, see NOTE at the bottom
of this file).

You must agree to the terms of these licenses, in addition to the COAST
source code license (Apache License, Version 2.0; see ./LICENSE), in order
to use this software.

Where a dependency is offered under multiple licenses, COAST is used under
the most permissive option (e.g. MIT is preferred over MPL-2.0, BSD is
preferred over GPL).

